> and I did rebuild them with the sh setup.sh command

Perhaps 'make clean' first and try again to be sure (though if it
fails at the linking stage this might not help much). Where in the
Makefile did you "replace" the path btw? IIRC, there's no
QTDIR=<something> in the Makefile, but $(QTDIR) is itself used..

If you have played too much with the Makefiles, perhaps replacing
$(SOMETHING)'s with directories (which you shouldn't do, generally),
you might want to extract the original Makefile and do a diff to see
what exactly you have changed.

When I compiled Nethack with Qt support last time (though it wan't for
Linux), I had to:

- #define QT_GRAPHICS in config.h

in Makefile.src:

- LINK=g++ (did you do this?)
- CXX=g++
- CXXFLAGS = ... -I$(QTDIR)/include
- WINSRC = ... $(WINQTSRC)
- WINOBJ = ... $(WINQTOBJ)
- WINLIB = ... $(WINQTLIB)

(These have to be the only assignments of the respective variables!)

